-- A proven-undetermined answer in a `compare` slot is the structural
-- `compare`, never the `eq` leaf (checker-v2.md §12.2, §13.1).
-- `S.eq` asks its element for `compare`, and the element of
-- `[ [] ]` is a type nothing determines; the record's derived `eq` is that
-- slot's nearest derived ancestor, so an `undetermined` leaf there would be
-- read by `Lower` as `eq` and hand `List.compare` the Bool-valued
-- `Basics.eq` (`List$compare(Basics$eq, …)`, harmless at run time only
-- because no value of the element type exists), and the evidence-count
-- assert refuses that. The table writes
-- `primitive num_compare`. Expected `yes`, `yes`.
--
-- Oracle twin: `run/UndeterminedUnderValueEvidence`'s `[ [] ] < [ [] ]`,
-- the same slot with no derived ancestor, answered with
-- `num_compare`.
import Node exposing (Program)
import S


main : Program
main =
    Node.printLines
        [ if { s = S.Sorted [ [] ] } == { s = S.Sorted [ [] ] } then "yes" else "no"
        , if ( S.Sorted [ [] ], 1 ) == ( S.Sorted [ [] ], 1 ) then "yes" else "no"
        ]
